"Blurry vision","Ves poco a tu alrededor","You see little around you","Debilidad","Weakness","Ligereza","Lightness","Ojo agudo","Sharp eye","Sanación","Healing","Savia de calafate","Calafate sap","Hierba del monte","Mountain herb","Comela con ","Eat it with ",". No sabés qué hace hasta probarla",". You don't know what it does until you try it","Hierba - ","Herb - "," (hasta el próximo piso)"," (until the next floor)","Se rompió el vínculo","The bond broke","La leyenda de las luces rojas","The legend of the red lights",
"Hace generaciones, el cielo se abrió y unas luces rojas trajeron a los dioses a la tierra. Enfurecidos, pelearon entre ellos, y de esa pelea nacieron montañas, ríos, heladas y vientos. Hoy las luces volvieron.","Generations ago, the sky opened and red lights brought the gods to earth. Enraged, they fought each other, and from that fight were born mountains, rivers, frosts and winds. Today the lights have returned.","En el Hain lo hacen los hombres disfrazados, pero el verdadero bajó con las luces rojas. En la caída arrancó árboles enteros con las manos, y por eso hay troncos caídos que tapan los caminos del bosque.",
"In the Hain he is played by disguised men, but the real one came down with the red lights. In his fall he tore out whole trees with his hands, and that is why fallen trunks block the forest paths.","No es del Hain, es una leyenda de los tiempos antiguos. Un gigante que comía gente, y Oala, su pariente, protegía a los suyos de él. Los Sasán le reventaron los ojos con sus hondas y se volvió una gran roca.","He is not from the Hain, he is a legend from ancient times. A giant who ate people, and Oala, his kin, protected her own from him. The Sasán burst his eyes with their slings and he turned into a great rock.",
"El cabezón rápido, el espíritu del viento. En el Hain lo hacen dos hombres pintados igual, uno a cada lado de la choza. El verdadero bajó con las luces rojas, y corría tan rápido que de su paso nacieron los vientos que sacuden el bosque.","The fast big-head, the spirit of the wind. In the Hain he is played by two men painted the same, one on each side of the hut. The real one came down with the red lights, and he ran so fast that the winds that shake the forest were born from his passing.","La del cono negro y las garras largas. En la caída hizo varar a las ballenas y abrió la costa con las manos.",
"She of the black cone and the long claws. In her fall she stranded the whales and opened the coast with her hands.","La mujer que vive bajo la tierra, la más temida del Hain. Cuando se enoja, devora a los hombres. En la caída abrió las grietas por donde sube el fuego.","The woman who lives beneath the earth, the most feared of the Hain. When she gets angry, she devours men. In her fall she opened the cracks where the fire rises.","Kre, la luna","Kre, the moon","Dirigía el Hain de las mujeres hasta que Kreen descubrió el engaño. Escapó al cielo con la cara quemada, y cuando su odio crece se tiñe de rojo. En la caída movió las mareas.",
"She led the women's Hain until Kreen discovered the deceit. She fled to the sky with a burned face, and when her hatred grows she turns red. In her fall she moved the tides.","Kreen, el sol","Kreen, the sun","El que descubrió el engaño de las mujeres y persigue a Kre sin alcanzarla nunca. En la caída, su calor derritió las nieves y nacieron los ríos.","He who discovered the women's deceit and chases Kre without ever reaching her. In his fall, his heat melted the snows and the rivers were born.",
"El que levanta murallas de hielo y hace caer el granizo y las piedras de la montaña. En la caída nacieron de él las heladas y los vientos fríos del sur.","He who raises walls of ice and brings down the hail and the stones of the mountain. In his fall, the frosts and the cold southern winds were born from him.","Aquél-allá-arriba, el que vive más allá de las estrellas. Nadie lo nombra en voz alta. Es el juez de los dioses, y solo él puede cerrar el cielo.","The-one-up-there, he who lives beyond the stars. Nobody says his name out loud. He is the judge of the gods, and only he can close the sky.",
"Nuevo relato","New tale"," - Libro de Kon (L)"," - Book of Kon (L)","Atajo abierto","Shortcut opened","Ya podés empezar en el Mundo ","You can now start in World ","El Shoort de la nieve","The Shoort of the snow","El séptimo Shoort","The seventh Shoort","El Shoort del sol naciente","The Shoort of the rising sun","El Shoort del viento","The Shoort of the wind","El más fuerte de los Shoorts","The strongest of the Shoorts","El Shoort de la sombra","The Shoort of the shadow","El Shoort de las rayas",
